After the last session, several questions were raised, and I will now address them. The first question concerns the proper air supply for fire pumps and fire fans. This topic will be covered in detail in a future specialized session on fire alarm systems and equipment coordination, but I’ll briefly explain it here.

There are three main methods to start a fire pump:
1. Via a pressure switch or flow switch;
2. Automatic activation signal sent by the fire alarm system upon confirming a fire;
3. Direct coordination through the fire control room.

It’s worth noting that in North America, there is no dedicated fire control room or full-time personnel on duty. Typically, personnel responsible for overall building maintenance also handle fire safety, building automation, and other tasks. This differs from domestic regulations, which require an independent fire control room staffed 24/7 by dedicated personnel.
